# Ambush B and the birthsign conversation (Imperial Subterrane). Baurus lets the group go ahead (29); Glenroy waits
# outside Room B (30); when the player steps into the CGTrigZoneAmbushB box the group walks in (32); Glenroy reaches the
# door (34) and two more assassins attack; when both are dead the quest sets 36. The player enters Room B (box
# CGTrigZoneEmperorBirthsign sets inAmbushBRoom), Glenroy and Baurus notice the player (40), the cut scene ends (42) and
# the Emperor force-greets with the Nine question; any answer sets 43, the birthsign menu opens, then he asks "What about
# me?" (45) and the group moves on (50).

# Stage 32 is set ONCE by the trigger box, so the case waits for Glenroy at marker D (30) before the player steps in.
# The Blades lock the Ambush A gate (00026C11, needs a key) behind them; the player goes through the broken wall and
# the caverns (ImperialDungeon04/05) and drops through the broken wall (idwallbroken01) into ImperialDungeon02. The
# trigger (000C7603, 2428 3915, z -498; box x 2408-2449, y 3710-4120, z -644..-352) hangs in that drop; its top is
# above the ceiling grate, so the player is placed inside its west part over the corridor floor (-736) and falls. The
# navmesh has no drop-down link here, so no walk can take this drop.
# The two rats that break through the wall (CGRatA1/A2, set on the player by the tutorial) are killed first, as a
# player does: left alive they kept attacking the god-mode player, and the Emperor and Glenroy, not yet out of
# earshot, stood watching the fight (ObserveCombat lines "Look out!" / "Watch out!") and never walked on (13a).
case ambush_b_trigger
run
CGRatA1.kill
CGRatA2.kill
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 30
run
player.moveto CGMarkerDGlenroy
wait 60
run
player.setpos x 2415
player.setpos y 3915
player.setpos z -600
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 32
end

# Glenroy reaches the Room B door (34). The two assassins CGAssassin05Ref / 06Ref attack the Blades; the player finishes
# them (kill stands in for the fight). CharGenQuest sets 36 when ambushCount reaches 2.
# Both die in the same instant on purpose: each assassin's own script adds 1 to the quest's ambushCount, which used
# to lose a count when two scripts added at once (run 6d: 36 never came). The converter now routes such adds through
# the owning script (TES4Add_<var>); 5 of 5 with the kills together (runs 9a).
# Five more assassins (CGGenericAssassin1-3, 0001774A, 00017734, same enable parent) wait on the road to F; they
# are fought there (walk_marker_f). Killing them from here did not hold: CGGenericAssassin1 was alive and
# shouting at F in run 13e.
case ambush_b_assassins
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 34
run
CGAssassin05Ref.kill
CGAssassin06Ref.kill
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 36
end

# The player walks into Room B: CGAmbushBMarker1 lies inside the CGTrigZoneEmperorBirthsign box (inAmbushBRoom = 1).
# Glenroy or Baurus detecting the player sets 40.
# The second drop: the player falls into Room B, whose trigger (000C7606, TrigZone01 x2.5 at 1395 5072 -944: box
# ~1040 square, z -1187..-701) fills the room. The player is placed above CGAmbushBMarker1 (1285 5169), just above
# the box top and below the ceiling grates (~-400), and falls in. No drop-down link exists here.

# Glenroy's reaction scene ends (INFO 000164B9 sets 42). The Emperor, in place in Room B, waits for the player and
# calls "Come closer. I'd prefer not to have to shout." (INFO 0004F791, GetDistance player >= 400); the player then
# walks up to him across Room B (a few hundred units; his force-greet ends the walk) and he greets: "They cannot
# understand why I trust you." The player answers the Nine question; all three answers set 43, whose fragment
# opens the birthsign menu. (Approaching on landing, stage 40, met him outside Room B, too far from Glenroy's
# escort to F; a teleport into his force-greet range gave no greeting or lost it: runs 1q, 1r, 1t, 1u.)
# ONE case from the drop into Room B to the question: once the player is in the room the quest waits for nobody,
# and the Emperor's say-once greeting can start before a case that ended at 40 has saved its checkpoint, which
# closes it and leaves only "I need your help. Please come with us." (run 6f). He calls "Come closer" only while
# the player is 400 away, so the case does not wait for that (6e: the player stood nearer and he greeted at once);
# it goes up to him and hears the greeting's LAST line. `approach`, not `walk`: the walk sometimes never arrived
# (6g), and `approach` leaves a conversation that is already opening alone (it used to teleport the player in the
# same tick the greeting opened, which closed it for good: runs 7a-7c, 8a).
# The Emperor can still be walking in from the corridor above the drop at 42 (floor -736; Room B floor -864). An
# `approach` then put the player back up there, where Baurus could not reach them for the torch greeting (11a,
# 11b: he stood on CGBaurusGreetPlayer 1038 away). From 36 the Emperor walks to CGMarkerEEmperor in Room B
# (CGEmperorToMarkerE, stage >= 32) and 42 freezes him wherever he is (CGEmperorToPlayerA waits in place; 12a: he
# stayed at z -665 for 3600 ticks). A player needs longer to find the drop than he needs to walk in, so the case
# waits for him at his marker before dropping in.
case ambush_b_nine_question
until 3600 UrielSeptimRef.GetDistance CGMarkerEEmperor < 300
run
player.setpos x 1285
player.setpos y 5169
player.setpos z -680
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 40
expect Charactergen.inAmbushBRoom == 1
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 42
expect UrielSeptimRef.GetPos z < -800
approach UrielSeptimRef
hear 900 UrielSeptimRef invisible hand
wait 30
ask "The Nine guide and protect us."
until 300 GetStage Charactergen >= 43
end

# Menu expected: the birthsign menu. TES4_Chargen.Ask hands it to MorrowindRuntime's chargen menu, so `pick` names the
# row (BSGN FULL); the MessageBox pages are only its fallback. The Emperor then re-greets (stage 44) with "The signs I read ..." and the
# player asks "What about me?" (his answer for the picked sign sets 45); CharGenQuest sets 50 after his speech.
# That answer offers "Can you see my fate?" and "Aren't you afraid to die?"; their answers offer each other and
# "Where are we going?" (needs Charactergen.fate and .die, set by the two answers), the only line with no choices.
# Since the force greet's exit hold (af21975f) Goodbye stays hidden until then, as in Oblivion.
case ambush_b_birthsign
pick The Warrior
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 44
hear 900 UrielSeptimRef The signs I read
wait 30
ask "What about me?"
ask "Can you see my fate?"
ask "Aren't you afraid to die?"
ask "Where are we going?"
bye
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 45
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 50
end
